  {
    "code": "MACRO-52",
    "status": "EXPERIMENTAL_CANDIDATE",
    "output": "tmp\\pdf_accessibility\\full_batch_v1\\layout_final\\after\\MACRO-52.pdf",
    "tagCount": 60,
    "mcids": 71,
    "unassignedMeaningfulBlocks": 0,
    "inlineFormulaSemantics": "SOURCE_BOUND_RUNS",
    "transcript": [
      {
        "role": "H1",
        "text": "International Transactions and Open-Economy Identities",
        "node": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "MACROECONOMICS",
        "node": 1
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "MACRO-52",
        "node": 2
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "Time: 6 minutes",
        "node": 3
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "Outcome: Calculate trade and capital balances and connect NX, NCO, saving, and investment.",
        "node": 4
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "Difficulty: Intermediate",
        "node": 5
      },
      {
        "role": "H2",
        "text": "THE CORE IDEA",
        "node": 6
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "Net exports are exports minus imports: NX = X - M. Positive NX is a trade surplus; negative NX is a trade deficit. Net capital outflow is domestic purchases of foreign assets minus foreign purchases of domestic assets. In the course accounting model, NX = NCO. National saving finances domestic investment and NCO, so S = I + NCO = I + NX.",
        "node": 7
      },
      {
        "role": "H2",
        "text": "HOW TO RECOGNIZE IT",
        "node": 8
      },
      {
        "role": "Lbl",
        "text": "-",
        "node": 11
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "Exports add to NX; imports subtract from NX.",
        "node": 12
      },
      {
        "role": "Lbl",
        "text": "-",
        "node": 14
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "A domestic resident buying a foreign asset raises capital outflow and NCO.",
        "node": 15
      },
      {
        "role": "Lbl",
        "text": "-",
        "node": 17
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "A foreign resident buying a domestic asset lowers NCO and is a capital inflow.",
        "node": 18
      },
      {
        "role": "Lbl",
        "text": "-",
        "node": 20
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "If S exceeds I, the difference is positive NCO and positive NX.",
        "node": 21
      },
      {
        "role": "H2",
        "text": "WATCH OUT",
        "node": 22
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "Do not import Micro tariff or comparative-advantage analysis into these identities. Also do not call a trade deficit a mathematical error: it corresponds to negative NCO in the accounting model.",
        "node": 23
      },
      {
        "role": "H2",
        "text": "WORKED EXAMPLE: MATCHING THE TWO SIDES",
        "node": 24
      },
      {
        "role": "H3",
        "text": "KEY RELATIONSHIPS",
        "node": 25
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "NX = exports - imports",
        "node": 28
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "NCO = domestic foreign-asset purchases - foreign domestic-asset purchases",
        "node": 30
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "NX = NCO",
        "node": 32
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "S = I + NCO",
        "node": 34
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "Therefore S = I + NX",
        "node": 36
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "Exports are $300 billion and imports are $360 billion, so NX = -$60 billion. Residents buy $90 billion of foreign assets while foreigners buy $150 billion of domestic assets, so NCO = $90 - $150 = -$60 billion. If investment is $240 billion, saving is I + NCO = $180 billion.",
        "node": 37
      },
      {
        "role": "H2",
        "text": "CHECK YOURSELF",
        "node": 38
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "National saving is $250 billion and investment is $210 billion. What are NCO and NX?",
        "node": 39
      },
      {
        "role": "H2",
        "text": "READY?",
        "node": 40
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "Return to the game and master this concept.",
        "node": 41
      }
    ],
