  {
    "code": "MICRO-60",
    "status": "EXPERIMENTAL_CANDIDATE",
    "output": "tmp\\pdf_accessibility\\full_batch_v1\\batches\\micro_later\\after\\MICRO-60.pdf",
    "tagCount": 42,
    "mcids": 45,
    "unassignedMeaningfulBlocks": 0,
    "inlineFormulaSemantics": "NO_INLINE_EXPRESSIONS_SELECTED",
    "transcript": [
      {
        "role": "H1",
        "text": "Adverse Selection",
        "node": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "MICROECONOMICS",
        "node": 1
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "MICRO-60",
        "node": 2
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "Time: 5 minutes",
        "node": 3
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "Outcome: Identify hidden-information problems that arise before an agreement or transaction.",
        "node": 4
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "Difficulty: Intermediate",
        "node": 5
      },
      {
        "role": "H2",
        "text": "THE CORE IDEA",
        "node": 6
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "Adverse selection arises when one side has private information about characteristics or risk before an agreement. Because prices or terms cannot fully reflect each type, higher-risk or higher-cost participants may be more likely to enter, changing the market pool.",
        "node": 7
      },
      {
        "role": "H2",
        "text": "HOW TO RECOGNIZE IT",
        "node": 8
      },
      {
        "role": "Lbl",
        "text": "-",
        "node": 11
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "Look for hidden characteristics or risk known by one party before agreement.",
        "node": 12
      },
      {
        "role": "Lbl",
        "text": "-",
        "node": 14
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "The informed and uninformed sides value the transaction differently because information is unequal.",
        "node": 15
      },
      {
        "role": "Lbl",
        "text": "-",
        "node": 17
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "When one price covers many types, high-risk or high-cost types may participate disproportionately.",
        "node": 18
      },
      {
        "role": "Lbl",
        "text": "-",
        "node": 20
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "The pool can worsen, raising prices, reducing coverage, or eliminating beneficial trade.",
        "node": 21
      },
      {
        "role": "H2",
        "text": "WATCH OUT",
        "node": 22
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "Do not confuse adverse selection with moral hazard. Adverse selection is hidden information before agreement; moral hazard is hidden action or changed behavior after protection.",
        "node": 23
      },
      {
        "role": "H2",
        "text": "WORKED EXAMPLE: AN INSURANCE RISK POOL",
        "node": 24
      },
      {
        "role": "H3",
        "text": "DIAGNOSE",
        "node": 25
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "hidden characteristics",
        "node": 28
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "before agreement",
        "node": 30
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "private risk",
        "node": 32
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "selection into the pool",
        "node": 34
      },
      {
        "role": "LBody",
        "text": "market response",
        "node": 36
      },
      {
        "role": "P",
        "text": "An insurer cannot perfectly observe applicants' health risk before enrollment, so it charges one premium based on average expected cost. Risk type already exists before coverage. Higher-risk applicants find the policy more attractive and enroll at a higher rate. The insured pool's expected cost rises, so the insurer may raise premiums or reduce coverage. Those responses can drive more low-risk buyers away, worsening selection.",
        "node": 37
      },
      {
        "role": "H2",
        "text": "CHECK YOURSELF",
        "node": 38
      },
      {
